6. The validity of such a direction came up for consideration before the Gujarat High Court in Special Civil Application No. 6495/1989 and batch (M/s.
Deepak Vegetable Oil Industries Ltd. v. Union of India
) decided by the Bench consisting of G. T. Nanavati and J. U. Mehta, JJ., by judgment dated 30-1-90/5-2-90. The Gujarat High Court in the aforesaid case took the view that the notification granting concession in payment of excise duty by taking credit in the use of minor oils the petitioner acted bona fide and on the belief that he was entitled to the concession in the notification and further that he will have a right to utilise the credit in terms of the said notification. This view was based on the ground Rule 57N continued to exist which conferred a right to credit for manufacture of Vanaspati from minor oils.
